The benefit side of the memo included expected deaths, expected injuries, and the value of vehicles that would otherwise be destroyed. Because the injury coefficient is garbled in the transcript, it is safest to keep that term symbolic: $\begin{aligned}
B_{\text{Pinto safety}}
&=180(\$200{,}000)+180I \\
&\quad+2000(\$700) \\
&\approx \$49.5\,\text{million}.
\end{aligned}$ where $I$ denotes the memo’s injury valuation. The decision then follows from the sign of the difference: $\begin{aligned}
\Delta_{\text{Pinto}}
&=B_{\text{Pinto safety}}-C_{\text{Pinto safety}} \nonumber\\
&\approx \$49.5\,\text{million}-\$137\,\text{million} \nonumber\\
&\approx -\$87.5\,\text{million}.\end{aligned}$ So the device is not installed.

